6. Conveying Non-Source Forms.

You may convey a covered work in object code form under the terms
of sections 4 and 5, provided that you also convey the
machine-readable Corresponding Source under the terms of this License,
in one of these ways:

a) Convey the object code in, or embodied in, a physical product
(including a physical distribution medium), accompanied by the
Corresponding Source fixed on a durable physical medium (or any other
medium), provided that the durably fixed medium and the physical
product are both available to the public.

b) Convey the object code in, or embodied in, a physical product
(including a physical distribution medium), accompanied by a written
offer, valid for at least three years, to give anyone who has a copy
of the object code the Corresponding Source in source code form.

c) Convey individual copies of the object code with a copy of the
Corresponding Source in a separate file. You must give the recipient
the opportunity to obtain the Corresponding Source by one of the
methods described in (a) or (b).

d) Convey the object code by offering access from a designated place
(which may be a network server), and offer equivalent access to the
Corresponding Source in the same way, at no charge.

e) Convey the object code using peer-to-peer transmission, provided
you inform other peers of the location of the Corresponding Source.

A separable portion of the object code, whose source code cannot be
derived from the object code, may be conveyed without the
Corresponding Source, provided that the separable portion was not
derived from the source code of the covered work, but is based on
other source code.

